{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1764775,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"Game of Code 4.0","festival_id":520881,"organization_id":943045,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-02T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-23T16:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/game-of-code-40-bharati-vidyapeeths-college-of-engineering-1764775","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>About the Event:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Game of Code 4.0<\/strong> is a premier competitive coding and problem-solving challenge organized by <strong>DSC x BMS BVCOE<\/strong>. Combining physical strategy, logical reasoning, and technical debugging, the event tests participants' teamwork, analytical thinking, and code-decoding skills under time pressure.<\/p>\n<p>Throughout the competition, clues and problem statements incorporate key themes from the <strong>United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)<\/strong>, promoting awareness of real-world sustainability issues through algorithmic thinking.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round Wise Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Treasure Hunt (Campus Strategy &amp; SDG Clues)<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Format: On-campus physical treasure hunt.<\/li>\n<li>Mechanism: Teams navigate the college premises by solving technical clues, logical riddles, and SDG-themed challenges. Each solved clue unlocks the location\/puzzle for the next checkpoint. Teams must work together and complete the route to qualify for the next stage.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Debug &amp; Decode (Paper-Based Technical Challenge)<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Format: Offline paper-and-pen coding sprint.<\/li>\n<li>Mechanism: Qualified teams receive printed code snippets, logical puzzles, syntax errors, and code-decoding challenges. Participants must manually trace execution, identify bugs, predict outputs, and write corrected logic within a strict time limit&mdash;no laptops or electronic devices permitted!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules and Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Eligibility: Open to college students and external participants.<\/li>\n<li>Team Structure: Participants must register in <strong>teams of exactly 3 members<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Identification: All participants must bring a valid student\/college ID card to the venue.<\/li>\n<li>Round 1 (Treasure Hunt) Conduct:\n<ul>\n<li>Teams must stick together at all times during the hunt.<\/li>\n<li>Running inside academic areas, pushing, trespassing into restricted areas, or disturbing ongoing college classes\/activities is strictly prohibited.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Round 2 (Debug &amp; Decode) Integrity:\n<ul>\n<li>No electronic devices or laptops are permitted during the paper-based round.<\/li>\n<li>Plagiarism, cheating, or receiving external help will lead to immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Evaluation &amp; Tie-Breakers:\n<ul>\n<li>Judging is based on solution correctness, total points scored, and completion speed.<\/li>\n<li>In the event of a tie, time-based performance or designated tie-breaker questions will determine the final rank.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>Final Authority: Participants must adhere to event discipline. The decision of the organizers and judges is final and binding.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div id=\"model-response-message-contentr_2eadc96ed423d39a\" class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel md-content enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color stronger tutor-markdown-rendering\" dir=\"ltr\" aria-busy=\"false\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n<div><strong data-path-to-node=\"0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Contact for Queries<\/strong><\/div>\n<br \/>\n<ul>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"1\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Pranshu Garg<\/strong> &mdash; +91 82873 03441<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"2\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Adwaith<\/strong> &mdash; +91 97172 75210<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"r